<?php

/**
 * What this plugin uses, and when each part starts.
 *
 * `wp zt add <name>` appends to this file, so a module works as soon as it is
 * copied. The entry file reads it with `$plugin->bootstrap()`.
 *
 * Everything the plugin is made of is here, and listing one is what builds it.
 * Nothing outside this file is ever built, so reading it tells you what the
 * plugin has -- and in what order it comes up.
 *
 * **The top level is for modules that do nothing until something asks.** A
 * module listed here is built as the plugin loads and then waits:
 *
 * ```
 * Path::class,
 * Views::class,
 * Options::class => static function ( Options $options ): void {
 *     $options->add_autoloaded_groups( array( 'reports' ) );
 * },
 * ```
 *
 * A class entry's value is the callback that configures it, run when the module
 * is built and before it boots. A module needing none is written bare.
 *
 * **A module that acts on its own goes under the hook it acts on.** The timing
 * is a heading over the modules that share it, said once:
 *
 * ```
 * '{{loaded_hook}}' => array(
 *     Log::class,
 *     AdminPages::class,
 * ),
 *
 * 'init' => array(
 *     PostTypes::class,
 *     Assets::class,
 * ),
 * ```
 *
 * `{{loaded_hook}}` is this plugin's own action, fired at the end of `run()`
 * once every module is built. It is the earliest heading that still has the
 * whole plugin behind it, and where a module belongs unless WordPress will not
 * accept its work that early -- a post type, a block or a meta key wants
 * `init`.
 *
 * A heading takes the same two class shapes, so a module needing a hook *and*
 * configuration is `'init' => array( Assets::class => $callback )`. Add
 * `:priority` to order a heading against everything else on that hook --
 * `'init:20'` runs behind the default 10.
 *
 * Leave a module that acts on its own at the top level and the plugin throws,
 * naming the headings: the top level promises it does nothing until asked, and
 * such a module cannot keep that promise.
 */

declare( strict_types=1 );

// Loaded by the plugin, never requested directly.
\defined( 'ABSPATH' ) || exit;

return array();
